1
00:00:00,933 --> 00:00:01,767
<i>Hello, Dad?
Did you get what I sent?</i>

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,267
<i>Yes, child, the logo
and the address.</i>

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,067
<i> Many operations have failed</i>

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:06,633
<i>because of them and their
companions.</i>

5
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:09,800
<i>It's a spy camera.
There's someone I need to catch.</i>

6
00:00:09,933 --> 00:00:10,800
<i> Sir, I have a feeling</i>

7
00:00:10,933 --> 00:00:12,967
<i>that Berdugo's laboratory
is here.</i>

8
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,200
<i> Aren't we going to talk about</i>

9
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:15,833
<i>what happened to us
in the North?</i>

10
00:00:15,967 --> 00:00:17,533
<i> Do you really think</i>

11
00:00:17,667 --> 00:00:19,233
<i>I'll believe you didn't know
I'd be excluded?</i>

12
00:00:19,367 --> 00:00:20,067
<i> Joey...</i>

13
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,167
<i> Sir Andrew.</i>

14
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,733
<i>I'll be the one
to take Joey home.</i>

15
00:00:22,867 --> 00:00:23,433
<i> I don't want you to.</i>

16
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:24,400
<i> Come on.</i>

17
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:26,533
<i>Tell your family
who you really are.</i>

18
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:27,967
<i> You are Berdugo!</i>

19
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:29,333
<i>This should help you relax.
[GROANS]</i>

20
00:00:29,467 --> 00:00:32,967
<i>What did you do, Ma'am Rebecca?
Ma'am Rebecca!</i>

21
00:00:51,767 --> 00:00:55,467
Quick, call an ambulance!
Ma'am Yvette! Come quickly!

22
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,267
It's Ma'am Rebecca!

23
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,467
- Ma'am!
- It's mommy!

24
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,367
- Mommy!
- Ma'am! Ma'am!

25
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,667
Mom, wake up!

26
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,567
- Mom! Wake up, Mommy!
- Ma'am, Ma'am!

27
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:08,800
Tomas, where are you?

28
00:01:08,967 --> 00:01:12,133
Let's take mommy
to the hospital.

29
00:01:12,267 --> 00:01:16,767
<i>You cannot live, Rebecca.
They cannot know the truth.</i>

30
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:20,933
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC]

31
00:01:21,067 --> 00:01:23,400
We don't have those parts.
There's no order yet.

32
00:01:23,533 --> 00:01:25,133
You better come back tomorrow.

33
00:01:25,267 --> 00:01:28,400
- Okay, tomorrow?
- Yes, tomorrow, come back.

34
00:01:30,767 --> 00:01:34,567
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPS]
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

35
00:01:36,267 --> 00:01:38,000
[ENGINE STARTS]
[REVVING]

36
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:48,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]
[REVVING]

37
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:15,667
Joey.

38
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:18,133
You were inside the room

39
00:02:18,267 --> 00:02:20,967
when the transaction
in the North happened, right?

40
00:02:22,467 --> 00:02:24,000
Did you see Berdugo?

41
00:02:25,433 --> 00:02:27,200
Were you be able
to identify him?

42
00:02:30,067 --> 00:02:31,900
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:32,033 --> 00:02:33,467
<i> If you permit, Berdugo.</i>

44
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:35,367
<i>[SHATTERS]
Oh my gosh.</i>

45
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,500
No.

46
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:39,333
You, do you know who Berdugo is?

47
00:02:42,900 --> 00:02:44,667
[GUN FIRING]

48
00:02:46,067 --> 00:02:47,367
Castro, let's go!

49
00:02:47,533 --> 00:02:53,533
[GUN FIRING]
[TIRES SCREECHING]

50
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:55,333
I didn't see his face.

51
00:02:56,867 --> 00:02:58,167
Joey, I'm sorry.

52
00:03:00,567 --> 00:03:04,367
I'm sorry for this late apology.

53
00:03:04,500 --> 00:03:09,100
I kept justifying my decisions
instead of apologizing.

54
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:11,067
And I know I hurt you.

55
00:03:12,500 --> 00:03:14,700
Many times, actually.

56
00:03:14,833 --> 00:03:16,667
For not telling you that...

57
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,300
Zoey was my ex.

58
00:03:19,933 --> 00:03:23,333
Or my negligence that kept you
out of operations.

59
00:03:25,367 --> 00:03:26,767
And lastly,

60
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:30,800
for breaking my promise
to find Berdugo.

61
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:41,467
[PHONE RINGING]

62
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,967
Dad?

63
00:03:43,100 --> 00:03:44,100
<i> Joey, my child.</i>

64
00:03:44,233 --> 00:03:47,700
Your Korean friend,
do you still talk to him?

65
00:03:47,833 --> 00:03:49,467
<i> Who? Jin Ho?</i>

66
00:03:49,867 --> 00:03:51,967
Not yet. Why?

67
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:56,133
Because you mentioned that
he suddenly disappeared, right?

68
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,767
That he stopped contacting you?

69
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:05,200
Maybe he already caught
the syndicate member

70
00:04:05,333 --> 00:04:06,600
he was looking for.

71
00:04:06,733 --> 00:04:09,100
The one you said
who killed Ramon?

72
00:04:09,233 --> 00:04:10,533
<i> Yes.</i>

73
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:14,533
Maybe he returned to Korea,
that's why he's gone.

74
00:04:14,667 --> 00:04:16,700
- Why are you asking?
- Nothing.

75
00:04:16,833 --> 00:04:20,867
I'm just thinking of another way
to track Berdugo.

76
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,200
<i> Maybe he really left.</i>

77
00:04:23,333 --> 00:04:25,733
All right, dear, thank you.

78
00:04:25,867 --> 00:04:27,100
Okay, Dad.

79
00:04:27,233 --> 00:04:28,400
Love you.

80
00:04:30,867 --> 00:04:35,633
Major Delgado is asking
about Jin Ho?

81
00:04:35,767 --> 00:04:36,733
Yes.

82
00:04:37,933 --> 00:04:42,000
He probably thinks Jin Ho could
be a bridge to find Berdugo.

83
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:48,967
But no,
I don't know where Jin Ho is.

84
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,567
Where could he be?

85
00:04:52,133 --> 00:04:56,333
Did Peter contact Jin Ho?

86
00:04:56,467 --> 00:04:59,800
No, Peter went back
to his province.

87
00:05:06,067 --> 00:05:16,033
[ENGINE WHIRRING]
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

88
00:05:20,033 --> 00:05:29,933
[WINDOW WHIRRING]
[MOTORCYCLE REVVING]

89
00:05:31,133 --> 00:05:32,933
[AMBULANCE SIREN WAILING]

90
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:34,067
Mom...

91
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:35,167
Mom, hurry...

92
00:05:36,433 --> 00:05:39,267
Mom...
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

93
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,800
Mom, fight, Mom.

94
00:05:43,467 --> 00:05:45,400
I'm Doctor Miguel,
what happened?

95
00:05:45,533 --> 00:05:47,567
She took a lot of medicine.

96
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:52,300
We don't know how much, Doc.
Her mouth was foaming.

97
00:05:52,433 --> 00:05:54,000
It's a possible drug overdose.

98
00:05:54,133 --> 00:05:55,667
BP, nurse.

99
00:05:55,800 --> 00:06:00,533
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

100
00:06:03,733 --> 00:06:13,700
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

101
00:06:23,833 --> 00:06:26,967
Okay, what's happening now
are the effects

102
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,267
of drug overdose that she took.

103
00:06:28,400 --> 00:06:31,833
Most likely, since everything
is slowing down with her...

104
00:06:31,967 --> 00:06:33,233
Did she take painkillers?

105
00:06:33,367 --> 00:06:35,067
Most likely, it's painkillers,
right?

106
00:06:36,667 --> 00:06:37,500
I don't know.

107
00:06:37,633 --> 00:06:38,367
I don't know anymore.

108
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,867
Okay, we will do our best.

109
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:40,933
Okay, we'll do our best.

110
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:42,767
Please save my mommy.

111
00:06:42,900 --> 00:06:44,267
Do everything for my mom,

112
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:45,200
- please.
- We will do our best.

113
00:06:45,333 --> 00:06:46,167
We'll do our best.

114
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:52,233
[SOBBING]

115
00:06:52,367 --> 00:06:58,333
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

116
00:06:58,467 --> 00:06:59,900
Clarissa!

117
00:07:00,033 --> 00:07:01,267
What happened?

118
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:04,500
Ma'am, I just boiled leaves
for her herbal medicine.

119
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:07,233
When I went to the room,
she had already collapsed,

120
00:07:07,367 --> 00:07:09,700
and the pills were scattered.

121
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:13,767
You were with mommy.
Why did you leave her alone?

122
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,833
Hon, you have to calm down.

123
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,033
Why did you neglect her?
What, Clarissa? Answer me!

124
00:07:19,167 --> 00:07:20,667
Hon, you have to calm down.

125
00:07:20,800 --> 00:07:22,467
Clarissa, just go home for now.

126
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,600
We'll take care of this.

127
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,867
We'll call you
when we have news.

128
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,267
Sir, I can wait.

129
00:07:28,400 --> 00:07:29,667
No, we'll handle it.

130
00:07:32,100 --> 00:07:33,267
Ma'am...

131
00:07:34,267 --> 00:07:39,100
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

132
00:07:39,733 --> 00:07:42,467
<i>[SIGHS]
It's sad, isn't it?</i>

133
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:44,900
Because they're leaving one
by one.

134
00:07:45,033 --> 00:07:47,567
I didn't even get
to say goodbye.

135
00:07:47,700 --> 00:07:50,100
That's okay. That's life.
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:07:50,267 --> 00:07:52,733
Of course,
we all have our own lives.

137
00:07:52,867 --> 00:07:56,567
We don't need to always be there
for each other, right?

138
00:07:58,300 --> 00:08:01,567
And besides, you didn't even
like them, right?

139
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:04,800
You just had no choice
because we had a mission.

140
00:08:04,933 --> 00:08:06,633
You're harsh.

141
00:08:06,767 --> 00:08:10,233
I really appreciated what
the four of us built.

142
00:08:10,367 --> 00:08:14,167
What happened to us
wasn't a joke.

143
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,933
We had so many experiences.

144
00:08:16,067 --> 00:08:19,400
And it wasn't easy for you
to understand them.

145
00:08:19,533 --> 00:08:21,467
Because they were like cats
and dogs.

146
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:23,533
They were always fighting.

147
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:29,267
Jin Ho and Peter, cat and dog.

148
00:08:29,400 --> 00:08:31,633
When you're around, cat, dog,
and rat.

149
00:08:31,767 --> 00:08:34,300
[CHUCKLES]
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

150
00:08:34,433 --> 00:08:36,033
You slipped that in.

151
00:08:36,167 --> 00:08:36,933
Rat?

152
00:08:37,067 --> 00:08:38,100
Yes.

153
00:08:39,433 --> 00:08:43,067
Well, it works because...

154
00:08:43,200 --> 00:08:44,400
I'm brainy.

155
00:08:44,533 --> 00:08:46,633
Wow, you even justified it.

156
00:08:46,767 --> 00:08:48,400
Yeah. But my face...

157
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,200
Rat-like.

158
00:08:51,333 --> 00:08:53,400
Very cute, yes.

159
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:54,433
[SQUEAKS]

160
00:08:54,600 --> 00:08:55,833
Is that right?

161
00:08:55,967 --> 00:08:58,833
Is that right?
[SQUEAKING]

162
00:08:58,967 --> 00:09:01,867
But you know, not a rat, right?

163
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,800
- Cute.
- Okay, then not!

164
00:09:04,933 --> 00:09:06,433
You're defensive.

165
00:09:06,567 --> 00:09:08,000
Affected?

166
00:09:08,133 --> 00:09:09,600
Wow.

167
00:09:09,733 --> 00:09:12,333
Okay, fine, I'm not a rat.

168
00:09:13,733 --> 00:09:14,933
Really?

169
00:09:15,067 --> 00:09:16,967
And we're good now.

170
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:18,533
What do you mean good?

171
00:09:18,667 --> 00:09:21,567
Wait, why are you angry?
You've been shouting.

172
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,867
And why would I choose
to be angry?

173
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,333
Jin Ho and Peter are gone.

174
00:09:26,467 --> 00:09:29,233
I'm the only one left.
And you're still mad.

175
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:32,333
But...
[PHONE RINGING]

176
00:09:33,867 --> 00:09:35,300
Wait.

177
00:09:35,433 --> 00:09:36,333
Brainy.

178
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:39,600
Hello, Yvette?

179
00:09:39,733 --> 00:09:40,833
Andrew...

180
00:09:40,967 --> 00:09:42,033
It's about mommy...

181
00:09:42,167 --> 00:09:43,367
What happened to her?

182
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:45,267
Just come to the hospital.

183
00:09:45,400 --> 00:09:47,267
Hurry, please.

184
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:48,333
Okay.

185
00:09:48,467 --> 00:09:52,033
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

186
00:09:52,167 --> 00:09:53,667
They said mommy is in
the hospital.

187
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:55,033
What?

188
00:09:55,167 --> 00:09:56,600
Go see her.

189
00:09:56,733 --> 00:09:58,067
Be careful, okay?

190
00:09:58,200 --> 00:09:58,800
Okay.

191
00:09:58,933 --> 00:09:59,767
You be careful too.

192
00:09:59,900 --> 00:10:01,700
Thanks again.

193
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:07,467
[SUSPENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

194
00:10:24,067 --> 00:10:34,033
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

195
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:38,633
[PHONE RINGING]

196
00:10:38,767 --> 00:10:39,867
Cruz?

197
00:10:40,367 --> 00:10:41,400
<i> Major...</i>

198
00:10:41,533 --> 00:10:44,933
Chief asked me to call to you.
You needed something?

199
00:10:45,067 --> 00:10:47,067
I have something I want you
to find.

200
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:50,367
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:10:50,500 --> 00:10:51,467
Mom...

202
00:10:51,600 --> 00:10:53,533
Drink this first.

203
00:10:55,667 --> 00:10:56,967
- My child...
- Mom.

204
00:10:57,100 --> 00:10:59,467
Child, this is my fault,
it's my fault.

205
00:10:59,600 --> 00:11:02,000
I told Ma'am Rebecca
I'd only be gone a moment,

206
00:11:02,133 --> 00:11:03,400
but I did so many things.

207
00:11:03,533 --> 00:11:06,000
I even went to the kitchen.
I fixed so many things.

208
00:11:06,133 --> 00:11:06,633
- Mom.
- I should...

209
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:07,867
I should have said...

210
00:11:08,033 --> 00:11:09,833
I should have checked her first
before doing all that.

211
00:11:09,967 --> 00:11:11,700
It's not your fault.

212
00:11:11,833 --> 00:11:14,533
This is exactly what happened
with your father,

213
00:11:14,667 --> 00:11:16,633
when we thought he was gone.

214
00:11:16,767 --> 00:11:20,567
And I didn't even call him.
I didn't do anything.

215
00:11:20,700 --> 00:11:22,933
Mom, what happened happened.

216
00:11:23,067 --> 00:11:25,600
You didn't fail.
It's not your fault.

217
00:11:25,733 --> 00:11:28,367
Don't blame yourself.
Drink some water first.

218
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:29,367
What will I do?

219
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,367
I wouldn't be able handle it

220
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,667
if something happens
to Ma'am Rebecca.

221
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,800
I don't know how I'll face

222
00:11:34,933 --> 00:11:37,867
Ma'am Yvette and Sir Andrew,
child.

223
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:40,233
Mom, breathe first.

224
00:11:40,367 --> 00:11:41,767
One step at a time, Mom.

225
00:11:41,933 --> 00:11:43,133
Think of this for now...

226
00:11:43,267 --> 00:11:45,667
Ma'am Rebecca is already in
the hospital and being treated.

227
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:47,600
That's what's important, right?

228
00:11:48,667 --> 00:11:51,933
- This is my fault.
- It's not your fault, Mom.

229
00:11:53,667 --> 00:11:57,533
Why did I leave her?
I shouldn't have left her.

230
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,300
Mom...

231
00:12:00,433 --> 00:12:02,033
Drink this first.

232
00:12:03,433 --> 00:12:10,400
[SOBBING]
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

233
00:12:13,667 --> 00:12:15,533
I really checked many times.

234
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:17,767
No Lee Jin Ho in the database.

235
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:19,633
Not in police national records.

236
00:12:19,767 --> 00:12:21,100
Even Interpol notice

237
00:12:21,233 --> 00:12:23,167
and Foreign Liaison records,
nothing.

238
00:12:23,300 --> 00:12:24,633
Zero hits, Sir.

239
00:12:24,767 --> 00:12:26,533
That means only two things.

240
00:12:26,667 --> 00:12:29,633
Either his operation is illegal
or off the books.

241
00:12:29,767 --> 00:12:30,967
Black operations?

242
00:12:31,833 --> 00:12:34,333
I don't think so.
Even that has a footprint.

243
00:12:34,467 --> 00:12:36,067
A handler.

244
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,933
An entry clearance.

245
00:12:38,067 --> 00:12:40,133
But here, it's blank.

246
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
You know,
that only means one thing.

247
00:12:44,133 --> 00:12:48,900
That's not his real name
and he's not Korean police.

248
00:12:49,067 --> 00:12:50,967
Then who is this Korean?

249
00:12:53,067 --> 00:12:54,467
I don't know.

250
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:58,433
And why is he here chasing
the syndicate?

251
00:13:02,267 --> 00:13:03,733
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

252
00:13:03,867 --> 00:13:05,367
Yvette, where's mommy?

253
00:13:06,667 --> 00:13:08,500
The medical team is attending
to her.

254
00:13:08,633 --> 00:13:09,600
Where?

255
00:13:09,733 --> 00:13:13,500
Clarissa found her unconscious,

256
00:13:13,633 --> 00:13:16,200
foaming at the mouth,
in her room.

257
00:13:16,333 --> 00:13:21,033
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

258
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,733
- Mom...
- Doc...

259
00:13:24,867 --> 00:13:25,967
Sir, Ma'am.

260
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:27,533
How's my mommy?

261
00:13:27,667 --> 00:13:30,533
Well, she's in critical
condition.

262
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:33,233
We're still currently trying
to stabilize her.

263
00:13:33,367 --> 00:13:36,600
Her BP's at 64/40,
way below normal.

264
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:38,833
Her cardiac rate is only at 13,

265
00:13:38,967 --> 00:13:41,933
and she's only breathing
at 50 percent rate.

266
00:13:42,067 --> 00:13:44,200
The amount of drugs
she took earlier

267
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:45,800
really took a toll on her.

268
00:13:45,933 --> 00:13:47,100
Most likely,

269
00:13:47,233 --> 00:13:50,600
we will need to bring her to
the ICU and also detoxify her.

270
00:13:50,733 --> 00:13:54,333
But as of now, we are still
trying to stabilize her.

271
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:56,933
That is the current state
we are right now.

272
00:13:59,767 --> 00:14:02,367
Wait, why is mommy overdosed?

273
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:05,067
Andrew, it's her medication.

274
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:07,167
And given the quantity,

275
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,867
it looks intentional.

276
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,767
Take that back, Tomas.
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:15,700
- Mommy couldn't do that.
- Andrew, stop, please.

278
00:14:15,833 --> 00:14:19,067
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING RAPIDLY]

279
00:14:19,200 --> 00:14:20,833
- Doc?
- Mom?

280
00:14:22,667 --> 00:14:24,000
<i> Let's start CPR.</i>

281
00:14:24,133 --> 00:14:27,033
Nurse, do an EPI.
Intubate, okay?

282
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:31,867
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING RAPIDLY]

283
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:32,800
Mom...

284
00:14:33,867 --> 00:14:35,667
Mom, fight, please.

285
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:36,933
Mom...

286
00:14:37,067 --> 00:14:43,200
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

287
00:14:45,333 --> 00:14:46,867
Mom...

288
00:14:48,100 --> 00:14:52,833
[FLATLINING]
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

289
00:15:07,067 --> 00:15:08,200
<i> It's my fault.</i>

290
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:10,567
<i>I told Ma'am Rebecca
I'd only be gone a moment,</i>

291
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:12,100
<i> but I did so many things.</i>

292
00:15:12,233 --> 00:15:14,400
<i>I even went to the kitchen.
I fixed so many things.</i>

293
00:15:14,533 --> 00:15:15,700
<i> Mom, Mom...</i>

294
00:15:15,833 --> 00:15:17,600
<i>I should have checked her
first before doing all that.</i>

295
00:15:17,733 --> 00:15:19,367
<i> It's not your fault.</i>

296
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:23,400
<i>You just had no choice
because we had a mission then.</i>

297
00:15:23,533 --> 00:15:26,633
<i>I really appreciated
what the four of us built.</i>

298
00:15:26,767 --> 00:15:29,633
<i>What happened to us
wasn't a joke.</i>

299
00:15:29,767 --> 00:15:32,900
<i>Jin Ho and Peter, they're like
cats and dogs.</i>

300
00:15:33,033 --> 00:15:35,167
<i>But when you're around, it would
be a cat, dog, and rat.</i>

301
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:39,233
<i> It works because I'm brainy.</i>

302
00:15:39,367 --> 00:15:40,733
<i> Rat-like.</i>

303
00:15:44,633 --> 00:15:46,100
<i> Clear!</i>

304
00:15:48,500 --> 00:15:53,767
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]
[DRAMATIC MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:54,900
[SOBBING]

306
00:15:55,033 --> 00:15:56,833
Miss Rebecca was revived.

307
00:15:56,967 --> 00:15:58,733
She's unresponsive.

308
00:15:58,867 --> 00:16:02,333
In short, in layman's terms,
she's in a coma.

309
00:16:02,467 --> 00:16:06,100
We need to put her in the ICU
and detox her.

310
00:16:06,233 --> 00:16:09,567
As to how long she'll be
like this, I cannot say yet.

311
00:16:09,733 --> 00:16:11,667
I'll have the ICU ready.

312
00:16:11,800 --> 00:16:18,300
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

313
00:16:19,900 --> 00:16:21,167
Mom...

314
00:16:23,033 --> 00:16:24,767
Can you hear me?

315
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:29,267
Mom, fight, please, okay?

316
00:16:31,700 --> 00:16:34,167
We will never leave you here.

317
00:16:36,200 --> 00:16:37,767
Mom, fight.

318
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,567
Mom, I can't bear to lose you.

319
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:49,067
[DRAMATIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

320
00:16:54,667 --> 00:17:04,633
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

321
00:17:15,667 --> 00:17:20,067
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

322
00:17:21,833 --> 00:17:25,467
<i>It's sad, isn't it?
They're leaving one by one.</i>

323
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:27,367
<i>I didn't even get
to say goodbye.</i>

324
00:17:27,500 --> 00:17:29,400
<i>Of course,
we all have our own lives.</i>

325
00:17:29,533 --> 00:17:39,500
<i>We don't need to always
be there for each other, right?</i>

326
00:17:40,633 --> 00:17:43,967
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

327
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,533
Yvette...

328
00:18:24,467 --> 00:18:30,900
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

329
00:18:32,433 --> 00:18:36,267
Can we see mom in the ICU later?

330
00:18:36,400 --> 00:18:38,233
Tomas said...

331
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,600
we can look for a bigger
hospital.

332
00:18:41,700 --> 00:18:44,500
Yvette, do you believe
what Tomas said?

333
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:49,000
Honestly, I don't.

334
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:54,500
I believe mommy couldn't commit
suicide.

335
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:59,167
Among us, she was always
the strong one, right?

336
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:01,533
Even when she was sick.

337
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:05,067
Like I said,

338
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:08,467
she often stared blankly,
zoning out.

339
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:13,067
I don't know if it's the meds
or something else.

340
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,833
So, do you think...

341
00:19:20,233 --> 00:19:22,400
Mommy could really do that?

342
00:19:24,267 --> 00:19:27,600
I don't know, okay?
I don't know.

343
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:30,367
All of these are just
assumptions,

344
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:31,733
so I don't know.

345
00:19:31,867 --> 00:19:35,067
[SOBBING]

346
00:19:36,833 --> 00:19:39,033
Yvette stop, please.

347
00:19:39,167 --> 00:19:40,400
You need to go home.

348
00:19:40,533 --> 00:19:42,300
- No, I won't...
- Rest, Yvette.

349
00:19:42,433 --> 00:19:45,133
I won't leave mommy.

350
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:46,933
I'm not gonna leave her.

351
00:19:47,067 --> 00:19:48,500
I'm not gonna leave mommy.

352
00:19:48,633 --> 00:19:50,700
I'm sure there's nothing
we can do.

353
00:19:53,367 --> 00:19:55,067
Mommy is still in a coma.

354
00:19:56,533 --> 00:19:58,967
Also, maybe the kids are looking
for you.

355
00:19:59,833 --> 00:20:00,800
Yvette...

356
00:20:02,267 --> 00:20:05,733
No, I won't leave mommy.

357
00:20:05,867 --> 00:20:10,633
[SOBBING AND WHIMPERING]

358
00:20:14,533 --> 00:20:19,233
[MIMICS PUNCHES SWOOSHING]

359
00:20:20,467 --> 00:20:21,867
[SIGHS]

360
00:20:23,633 --> 00:20:25,200
[SIGHS]

361
00:20:37,933 --> 00:20:47,900
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:20:52,667 --> 00:20:55,333
Still mad I haven't introduced
you to Berdugo?

363
00:20:55,467 --> 00:20:58,300
Does it bother you that you're
still not a part of us?

364
00:20:59,567 --> 00:21:00,833
Listen.

365
00:21:01,967 --> 00:21:04,400
I handled Korean buyers,

366
00:21:04,533 --> 00:21:07,167
and I moved shipments
after port sweep,

367
00:21:07,300 --> 00:21:09,867
but I still haven't met Berdugo.

368
00:21:10,033 --> 00:21:11,967
You're impatient.

369
00:21:12,100 --> 00:21:13,367
No.

370
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:15,033
I'm underused.

371
00:21:15,167 --> 00:21:19,500
I want to be in the room
where decisions are made.

372
00:21:19,633 --> 00:21:22,000
Trust is layered, Jin Ho.

373
00:21:22,133 --> 00:21:23,400
Trust?

374
00:21:23,533 --> 00:21:24,967
[SCOFFS]

375
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:29,000
I left my country for you.

376
00:21:34,933 --> 00:21:44,300
Now, I'm burning bridges
for this organization!

377
00:21:44,467 --> 00:21:47,400
Berdugo doesn't show himself
to ambition.

378
00:21:47,533 --> 00:21:49,833
He doesn't just appear,

379
00:21:49,967 --> 00:21:52,667
especially to someone
who's still being...

380
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:54,300
tested.

381
00:21:56,233 --> 00:21:58,100
You want to meet him?

382
00:22:00,233 --> 00:22:01,733
Prove you can wait.

383
00:22:01,867 --> 00:22:11,833
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

384
00:22:24,600 --> 00:22:27,000
You and Lisa will handle
the operation for now.

385
00:22:27,133 --> 00:22:31,067
<i>I know it's heavy,
but I trust you can manage.</i>

386
00:22:31,200 --> 00:22:33,533
Will you be okay there, Boss?

387
00:22:33,667 --> 00:22:36,133
You should have finished
her off.

388
00:22:36,267 --> 00:22:37,533
I should have...

389
00:22:37,667 --> 00:22:39,200
<i>if she wasn't my wife's mother.</i>

390
00:22:39,333 --> 00:22:41,700
But anything more aggressive
would have...

391
00:22:41,833 --> 00:22:43,000
<i> raised questions.</i>

392
00:22:43,133 --> 00:22:46,033
So, nothing that would trigger
an autopsy or a paper trail.

393
00:22:46,167 --> 00:22:48,633
So, you'll make it look
like suicide?

394
00:22:48,800 --> 00:22:49,667
<i>Yes, that way there's
no complications.</i>

395
00:22:49,800 --> 00:22:51,667
Given her condition
and medications,

396
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:54,600
<i>authorities will read it
as trauma or psychosis.</i>

397
00:22:54,733 --> 00:22:56,700
Tomas?

398
00:22:56,833 --> 00:23:06,800
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

399
00:23:07,133 --> 00:23:11,867
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

400
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,767
I'm so confused who she wanted
to catch.

401
00:23:14,900 --> 00:23:17,800
Who could it be?
Ma'am Yvette? Sir Tomas?

402
00:23:17,933 --> 00:23:19,100
The teddy bear.

403
00:23:19,233 --> 00:23:19,767
Teddy bear?

404
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:21,167
It had a spy camera.

405
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,167
I'm sure it recorded
what really happened.

406
00:23:24,333 --> 00:23:26,167
Did you notice a teddy bear?

407
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:28,267
- It was thrown in the trash.
- What?

408
00:23:28,400 --> 00:23:30,233
Be careful, Major. Remember...

409
00:23:30,367 --> 00:23:32,267
The syndicate thinks
you're dead.

410
00:23:32,400 --> 00:23:34,367
Are you sure your informant
hangs out here?

411
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:35,100
Jin Ho?

412
00:23:35,233 --> 00:23:36,200
Just standby.

413
00:23:36,333 --> 00:23:38,533
Maybe he'll try to escape.
We can chase him.
